WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.260
Blackburn chose four measurements for his formula that you can easily look up on the web.

00:04.760 --> 00:10.640
Or measure yourself with a tape measure. First is R, the radius of your car's curb-to-curb

00:10.640 --> 00:15.540
turning circle, which is the distance from the front wheel E to the turning center X.

00:16.200 --> 00:21.140
Second is L, the wheelbase between the front wheel E and rear wheel F.

00:21.740 --> 00:27.340
Third is K, the front overhang from the front wheel E to the front bumper corner A.

00:27.340 --> 00:32.940
And fourth is W, the width GH of the parked car in front of you.

00:33.460 --> 00:36.340
Our goal is to find the extra distance AH.

